# Runtime-to-empty idle-current floor — hardware validation (NUCLEO-L476RG, extADC+BLE+INA219 rig)

Board: NUCLEO-L476RG  ·  Build: build-stm32-extadc-rte
Config: nucleo_l476rg_ble_extadc.conf + -DCONFIG_BATTERY_RUNTIME_TO_EMPTY=y
Wire: v5 (38 B)  ·  Serial console: /dev/cu.usbmodem1203 @ 115200
Date: 2026-06-06

## Problem

When a steady discharge load is removed, the EMA-smoothed current decays toward
zero through arbitrarily small positive values. With the original idle gate
(CONFIG_BATTERY_RUNTIME_IDLE_THRESHOLD_MA_X100 = 0, i.e. only current <= 0 is
"idle"), remaining_charge / tiny_current briefly produced multi-year RTE values
before the EMA crossed zero and the estimate became n/a. On the Grafana
"Time to Empty" panel this is a momentary spike to ~1.3M minutes.

## BEFORE (floor = 0) — load lifted, RL off INA219 VIN-

[v5 t=268302] ... I=0.10 mA Q=217.97 mAh RTE=261564 min     <- ema ~= 0.05 mA
[v5 t=270304] ... I=0.10 mA Q=217.97 mAh RTE=1307820 min    <- ema ~= 0.01 mA (~2.5 years)
[v5 t=272306] ... I=0.10 mA Q=217.97 mAh RTE=n/a            <- ema <= 0, settled

## FIX

Default CONFIG_BATTERY_RUNTIME_IDLE_THRESHOLD_MA_X100 0 -> 50 (0.50 mA), in both
the Kconfig (app/Kconfig.battery) and the C #ifndef fallback (battery_runtime.c).
A smoothed current at/below 0.50 mA is treated as idle -> NOT_AVAILABLE. This sits
above the current sensor's ~0.1 mA noise floor and bounds the largest emittable
estimate to remaining_charge / floor. Still Kconfig-tunable (0 = legacy behavior).

## AFTER (floor = 0.50 mA) — load lifted, RL off INA219 VIN-

[v5 t=58090] ... I=0.10 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=3528 min
[v5 t=60092] ... I=0.10 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=5112 min
[v5 t=62095] ... I=0.00 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=7294 min
[v5 t=64097] ... I=0.00 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=10401 min
[v5 t=66099] ... I=0.10 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=15336 min
[v5 t=68101] ... I=0.10 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=23004 min       <- peak, at the Q/floor bound
[v5 t=70103] ... I=0.10 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=n/a             <- settled
[v5 t=72105] ... I=0.10 mA Q=199.37 mAh RTE=n/a

Peak transient 23004 min (~16 days) vs old 1307820 min (~2.5 years): 83x smaller,
and matches the predicted bound Q/floor = 199.37 mAh / 0.5 mA * 60 = 23924 min.

## Steady-state under load (~30 mA) still correct after the fix

[v5 t=12044] ... I=29.60 mA Q=199.66 mAh RTE=404 min   (199.66/29.6*60 = 404.7)

## Tests

25 C host suites pass (test_runtime: below_floor/at_floor -> n/a, just_above_floor
reports, estimate never collides with the v5 sentinel). 122 gateway tests pass.
Build/config drift guard in sync.
